t usually need treatment with aciclovir.  Management is symptomatic with fluids and pain relief. Oral aciclovir, $200\mathrm{mg}\times5/\mathrm{d}$ ay for 5 days, is helpful in $1^{\circ}$ attacks if vesicles are still present (within the first 3 days). Recurrent herpes labialis does not usually need treatment with aciclovir.

