Patients with psoriasis have an increased risk of developing other inflammatory diseases that are immunologically mediated—seronegative arthritis (psoriatic arthritis——see $spadesuit$ p. 206) and Crohn disease. Case control studies have also shown an increased prevalence of the metabolic syndrome (see Box 9.2) in patients with psoriasis, possibly related to chronic inflammation and circulating inflammatory cytokines, including TNF- $upalpha$ . The psychosocial burden of psoriasis is considerable. Anxiety and depression are common, and patients tend to smoke and drink too much alcohol. Treat the whole patient, remembering associated co-​morbidities, including coeliac disease, cardiovascular disease (see ${sf B o x9.2p}$ . 191), hypertension, obesity, type 2 diabetes, peptic ulcer, and liver disease.  Patients with psoriasis have an increased risk of developing other inflammatory diseases that are immunologically mediated—seronegative arthritis (psoriatic arthritis——see $\spadesuit$ p. 206) and Crohn disease. Case control studies have also shown an increased prevalence of the metabolic syndrome (see Box 9.2) in patients with psoriasis, possibly related to chronic inflammation and circulating inflammatory cytokines, including TNF- $\upalpha$ . The psychosocial burden of psoriasis is considerable. Anxiety and depression are common, and patients tend to smoke and drink too much alcohol. Treat the whole patient, remembering associated co-​morbidities, including coeliac disease, cardiovascular disease (see ${\sf B o x9.2p}$ . 191), hypertension, obesity, type 2 diabetes, peptic ulcer, and liver disease.
